Shell utility to work with YT system.

Cypress (metainformation tree) commands:
    exists, list, find, create, get, set, remove, copy, move, link,
    concatenate, externalize, create-account, create-pool
File commands:
    read-file, write-file
Table commands:
    read-table, read-blob-table, write-table, create-temp-table,
    alter-table, get-table-columnar-statistics, dirtable
Dynamic table commands:
    mount-table, unmount-table, remount-table, freeze-table, unfreeze-table, get-tablet-infos,
    reshard-table, reshard-table-automatic, balance-tablet-cells, trim-rows, alter-table-replica,
    select-rows, explain-query, lookup-rows, insert-rows, delete-rows, get-tablet-errors
Run operation commands:
    erase, merge, sort, map, reduce, join-reduce, remote-copy, vanilla, map-reduce
Operation commands:
    abort-op, suspend-op, resume-op, complete-op, update-op-parameters,
    get-operation, list-operations, track-op
Job commands:
    run-job-shell, run-job-shell-command, abort-job, get-job-stderr,
    get-job-input, get-job-input-paths, get-job, list-jobs
Transaction commands:
    start-tx, commit-tx, abort-tx, ping-tx,
    lock, unlock
ACL (permission) commands:
    check-permission, add-member, remove-member
Operation tools:
    shuffle, transform
Diagnostics:
    job-tool, download-core-dump
Other commands:
    show-spec, execute, execute-batch, sky-share, show-default-config, transfer-account-resources, transfer-pool-resources,
    generate-timestamp
Subtools:
    chyt, spyt, jupyt, idm, flow

positional arguments:
  command
    exists              checks if Cypress node exists
    list                lists directory (map_node) content. Node type must be "map_node"
    find                searches for some nodes in Cypress subtree
    create              creates Cypress node
    create-account
    create-pool
    read                reads rows from table and parse (optionally)
    read-table          reads rows from table and parse (optionally)
    write               writes rows from input_stream to table
    write-table         writes rows from input_stream to table
    create-temp-table   creates temporary table by given path with given prefix and return name
    read-blob-table     reads file from blob table
    read-file           downloads file from path in Cypress to local machine
    download            downloads file from path in Cypress to local machine
    write-file          uploads file to destination path from stream on local machine
    upload              uploads file to destination path from stream on local machine
    get                 gets Cypress node content (attribute tree)
    set                 sets new value to Cypress node
    set-attribute       sets attribute at given path
    copy                copies Cypress node
    move                moves (renames) Cypress node
    link                makes link to Cypress node
    remove              removes Cypress node
    remove-attribute    removes attribute at given path
    externalize         externalize cypress node
    internalize         internalize cypress node
    concatenate         concatenates cypress nodes. This command applicable only to files and
                        tables
    mount-table         mounts the table
    unmount-table       unmounts the table
    remount-table       remounts the table
    reshard-table       changes pivot keys separating tablets of a given table
    reshard-table-automatic
                        automatically balance tablets of a mounted table according to tablet
                        balancer config
    balance-tablet-cells
                        reassign tablets evenly among tablet cells
    trim-rows           trim rows of the dynamic table
    alter-table         performs schema and other table meta information modifications
    freeze-table        freezes the table
    unfreeze-table      unfreezes the table
    get-tablet-infos    returns various runtime tablet information
    get-tablet-errors   returns dynamic table tablet and replication errors
    alter-table-replica
                        changes mode and enables or disables a table replica or replicated table
                        tracker for table replica
    select-rows         executes a SQL-like query on dynamic table
    select
    explain-query       explains a SQL-like query on dynamic table
    lookup-rows         lookups rows in dynamic table
    lookup
    insert-rows         inserts rows from input_stream to dynamic table
    insert
    delete-rows         deletes rows with keys from input_stream from dynamic table
    delete
    register-queue-consumer
                        registers queue consumer
    unregister-queue-consumer
                        unregisters queue consumer
    list-queue-consumer-registrations
                        lists queue consumer registrations
    pull-queue          reads rows from a single partition of a queue (i.e. any ordered dynamic
                        table)
    pull-consumer       reads rows from a single partition of a queue (i.e. any ordered dynamic
                        table) with authorization via consumer
    pull-queue-consumer
                        reads rows from a single partition of a queue (i.e. any ordered dynamic
                        table) with authorization via consumer
    advance-consumer    advances consumer offset for the given queue
    advance-queue-consumer
                        advances consumer offset for the given queue
    push-queue-producer
                        push rows to queue via queue producer
    create-queue-producer-session
                        creates queue producer session
    remove-queue-producer-session
                        removes queue producer session
    start-query         start query
    query               run query and track its progress (unless sync = false)
    abort-query         abort query
    read-query-result   read query result
    get-query           get query
    get-query-result    get query result
    get-query-tracker-info
                        get query tracker info
    list-queries        list operations that satisfy given options
    alter-query         alter query
    erase               erases table or part of it
    merge               merges source tables to destination table
    sort                sorts source tables to destination table
    map                 runs map operation
    reduce              runs reduce operation
    join-reduce         runs join-reduce operation
    map-reduce          runs map (optionally), sort, reduce and reduce-combine (optionally)
                        operations
    remote-copy         copies source table from remote cluster to destination table on current
                        cluster
    vanilla             run vanilla operation
    shuffle             shuffles table randomly
    abort-op            aborts operation
    suspend-op          suspends operation
    resume-op           continues operation after suspending
    track-op            synchronously tracks operation, prints current progress and finalize at
                        the completion
    complete-op         completes operation
    update-op-parameters
                        updates operation runtime parameters
    patch-op-spec       patches operation spec
    get-operation       get operation attributes through API
    list-operations     list operations that satisfy given options
    list-operation-events
                        list events of given operation
    check-operation-permission
                        check if user has permission for operation
    start-tx            starts transaction
    abort-tx            aborts transaction. All changes will be lost
    commit-tx           saves all transaction changes
    ping-tx             prolongs transaction lifetime
    lock                tries to lock the path. Do not forget about global `--tx` option
    unlock              tries to unlock the path
    add-member          adds member to Cypress node group
    remove-member       removes member from Cypress node group
    check-permission    checks permission for Cypress node
    get-table-columnar-statistics
                        gets columnar statistics of tables listed in paths
    execute-batch       executes `requests` in parallel as one batch request
    transfer-account-resources
                        transfers resources between accounts
    transfer-pool-resources
                        transfers resources between pools
    generate-timestamp  generates timestamp
    run-job-shell       runs interactive shell in the job sandbox
    run-job-shell-command
                        runs a command in the job sandbox and returns the output
    get-job-stderr      gets stderr of the specified job
    get-job-input       get full input of the specified job
    get-job-input-paths
                        get input paths of the specified job
    abort-job           interrupts running job with preserved result
    list-jobs           list jobs of operation
    get-job-trace       get traces of the specified job
    get-job-spec        get spec of the specified job
    get-job             get job of operation
    list-job-traces     list traces of the specified job
    set-user-password   updates user password, reading it and optionally a current password
    issue-token         issues a new token for user, reading password interactively and securely
                        from console
    revoke-token        revokes user token, reading password and maybe token value interactively
                        and securely from console
    list-user-tokens    lists sha256-encoded user tokens, reading password interactively and
                        securely from console
    whoami              invokes whoami command at YT API and returns login
    execute             the type of the None singleton
    transform           transforms source table to destination table writing data with given
                        compression and erasure codecs
    job-tool            Tool helps to debug user job code by preparing job environment on local
                        machine. It downloads all necessary job files, fail context (small
                        portion of job input data) and prepares run script.
    run-compression-benchmarks
                        Gets input table and recompresses it in all available codecs. For each
                        codec prints compression ratio, cpu_write and cpu_read.
    dump-parquet        dump table with a strict schema as `Parquet
                        <https://parquet.apache.org/docs>` file
    upload-parquet      upload `Parquet <https://parquet.apache.org/docs>` file as a table
    dump-orc            dump table with a strict schema as `ORC <https://orc.apache.org/>` file
    upload-orc          upload `ORC <https://orc.apache.org/>` file as a table
    show-default-config
                        returns default configuration of python API
    detect-porto-layer
    explain-id
    show-spec           shows available spec options of the operation
    download-core-dump  downloads core dump for a given operation_id and job_id from a given
                        core_table_path
    get-features        retrieves supported cluster features (data types, codecs etc.)
    run-command-with-lock
                        the type of the None singleton
    add-maintenance     adds maintenance request for a given node
    remove-maintenance  removes maintenance requests from given node by id or filter

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --proxy PROXY         specify cluster to run command, by default YT_PROXY from environment
  --prefix PREFIX       specify common prefix for all relative paths, by default YT_PREFIX from
                        environment
  --config CONFIG       specify configuration
  --tx TX               perform command in the context of the given transaction, by default
                        0-0-0-0
  --master-cell-id MASTER_CELL_ID
                        perform command in master specified by this id; supported only for native
                        driver and testing purposes
  --ping-ancestor-txs   turn on pinging ancestor transactions
  --trace               trace execution of request using jaeger
  --version             show program's version number and exit

Examples:

List content of root directory of Hume cluster and check access to system.
$  yt list / --proxy <cluster_host>
>> home
   sys
   tmp

Set YT_PROXY = <cluster_host> to avoid usage --proxy option.
$ export YT_PROXY=<cluster_host>
(Add this string to ~/.bashrc)

$  yt create table //tmp/sepulki
>> [...] Access denied: "write" permission for node //tmp is not allowed by any matching ACE [...]

Oops! Forgotten token. Follow https://ytsaurus.tech/docs/en/user-guide/storage/auth

$  yt create table //tmp/sepulki
>> 1-2-3-4

See all attributes created table.
$ yt get "//tmp/sepulki/@"
>> {
        "chunk_list_id" = "5c6a-1c2459-65-1f9943e3";
        "inherit_acl" = "true";
        [...]
    }

You can use GUID of object #1-2-3-4 instead path.
See also https://ytsaurus.tech/docs/en/user-guide/storage/ypath

Note! Create parent directory of table before writing to it. Recursive path creating is not available during operation.

Write to table in Cypress from local file.
$ cat my_data_in_json | yt write //tmp/sepulki --format json

For appending to table instead rewriting specify append mode.
$ cat my_data_in_yson | yt write '<append=true>//tmp/sepulki' --format yson

Output table to client stdout.
$ yt read //tmp/test_table --format dsv
>> b=hello  a=10
   b=world  a=20

Run map-reduce operation, append result to destination table.
$ yt map-reduce --mapper "python my_mapper.py" --map-local-file "~/my_mapper.py" --reducer "./my_reducer.pl" --reduce-file "//tmp/my_reducer.pl"
--src //project/some_existing_table  --src some_another_table_in_prefix_directory --dst <append=true>//tmp/sepulki
--reduce-by "column_one" --reduce-by "column_two"
>> [...] operation 5-6-7-8 initializing [...]

Sort the table.
$ yt sort --src //project/some_existing_table --dst //tmp/sepulki --sort-by "column-one"

Sort the table in descending order.
$ yt sort --src //project/some_existing_table --dst //tmp/sepulki --sort-by "{name=column-one; sort_order=descending;}"

Note! Without modification `append=true` destination table is overwritten.
Note! Specify paths to user scripts!

Lookup rows from dynamic table.
$ echo '{host=abc.com}' | yt lookup-rows //my/dynamic/table
>> {"host"="abc.com";"last_seen_time": "2017-04-10T12:35:10"}

